{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For.</b> The sense of כי is like כי עם־קשה ערף הוא (Exodus 34:9), but it means 'because of,' and the meaning is: because of Rezin and the son of Remaliah, those who besiege Jerusalem." "<b>And while.</b> As if to say, 'sixty-five years still remain, and it shall be so.' The supplementary bet is like the bet in בטרם. The beginning of this reckoning is from the year of the earthquake that was in the days of Uzziah, when Amos prophesied, ישראל גלה יגלה (Amos 7:11). Similarly, ויהי מקץ ארבעים שנה ויאמר אבשלום (2 Samuel 15:7)." "<b>shall be shattered.</b> From the root of החתות (Isaiah 9:3), and it is of the nifal pattern, like ימם (Isaiah 13:7). The meaning is that evil shall come upon him. And it is possible that יחת is of the forms whose [first] root letter is nun, like יגש, and similar is תחת גערה במבין (Proverbs 17:10). And behold, the nun appears in the phrase הנחת יי גבוריך (Joel 3:11), and the meaning is that he shall fall from being reckoned as a people."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:37.277964308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}